    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0540" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg456"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay acknowledges the receipt of Mr. White’s telegram mentioning the
                    President’s name as possible arbitrator, and states that <pb facs="0541" n="457"
                        xml:id="pg457"/> while the President would not decline any service which was
                    desired by the powers interested for the settlement of pending claims he would
                    like Mr. White to intimate, discreetly and unofficially, to the British minister
                    for foreign affairs that he would regard it as altogether desirable that the
                    matter should be referred to The Hague.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
